# YOU ALMOST CERTAINLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE.
#
# The client half ships INSIDE the Composer package, at
# `vendor/panelkit/panel/client/panelkit-client.tgz`. One credential installs
# both halves, there is no registry to reach, and the two can never be
# different versions:
#
#     composer require panelkit/panel
#     npm install ./vendor/panelkit/panel/client/panelkit-client.tgz @vitejs/plugin-vue
#
# THIS FILE IS FOR ONE CASE ONLY: pulling the client tarball from a GitHub
# Release on its own - a separate front-end build, or a machine that has no
# Composer install. Save it as `.npmrc` next to package.json:

//github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}

# The token is read from the environment, so this file holds no secret and can
# be committed. It needs `repo` scope to read a private repository's release
# assets.
#
# Then, with the URL from the Releases page:
#
#     npm install https://github.com/enterprisealxtexh/panelkit/releases/download/v0.9.2/alxtexh-enterprise-panel-0.9.2.tgz
#
# NOTE ON GITHUB PACKAGES, which this deliberately does not use: its npm
# registry requires a token even for PUBLIC packages. There is no anonymous
# read, so it can never be the frictionless option it looks like.
